{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-surface/src/tests/clax.d.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T05:05:01.708110Z","id":"d1ba730e120425014ed56e1d590ec36ece36ad0a1d491efd053c706157bdb5ee","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-surface may not read up into clax-bot, which owns the file. Its tests that only need some surface of Clax's own (reserved names, a declaration of two surfaces, `check_args` wording, kinds without `@allow`) read src/tests/clax.d.ts: 14 of ClaxBot's 24 operations and the interfaces they reach, copied when the file moved, and held equal to nothing. Moving those tests to clax-bot would leave one file, but they use the crate's private helpers (`shown_whole`, `model_text`, the two hosts' examples through //docs:claxbot_surface_examples), and would make clax-bot's tests the place where clax-surface's printer is tested. The tests about ClaxBot's file itself did move: crates/clax-bot/src/api.rs, `the_surface_file_is_read_as_written` and `the_surface_file_declares_what_the_goldens_do`.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":5},"content_hash":"2889dcda09f4b990e82cc73ad68668d483e043aeb0fe4f801cd4d27bd98cb8ba"},"summary":"Run the tests that want Clax's surface beside a host's in clax-bot, against crates/clax-bot/src/clax.d.ts, instead of keeping a part of it here","tags":["revisit:the fixture and ClaxBot's file disagree about a form a test here relies on","claxbot-surfaces","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-surface/src/tests/clax.d.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T06:03:09.306654Z","id":"c7e49c7878f9755739375b4bf91907f390a8a50ee18955ae6f9d8b37e14d0562","body":{"detail":"Commit \"test(surface): the tests' surface named clax is the crate's own fixture, own.d.ts\". The fixture stays in clax-surface (the alternative of this record is not taken). Its header and tests/mod.rs say that it is a surface named `clax` in the shape of one Clax provides itself, not crates/clax-bot/src/clax.d.ts, and that nothing holds the two equal; the tests read it through `own()` and `OWN_DTS`, and `claxs_own_surface_is_read_as_written` is `the_fixture_named_clax_is_read_as_written`.","kind":"comment","references":"d1ba730e120425014ed56e1d590ec36ece36ad0a1d491efd053c706157bdb5ee","summary":"The file this record is on is now crates/clax-surface/src/tests/own.d.ts, and says it is the crate's own fixture, free to differ from ClaxBot's file","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
